  "configuration_id": "config_020",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment should establish a strong baseline for the full multimodal pipeline. config_020 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) combines the most expressive choices across all dimensions: a learned biological latent (scvi_n200), a strong pretrained vision backbone (imagenet_vit_l), the most flexible aggregation (transformer), and a learned fusion (weighted). This tests the core hypothesis that multimodal fusion with rich representations outperforms simpler alternatives, and provides a high-performance anchor. If it performs well, subsequent experiments can ablate individual components to identify which matter most; if it underperforms, we learn that complexity is not the bottleneck and can pivot toward simpler or modality-specific designs. This is the highest-information-gain first experiment under a 10-run budget."
}

